      "subject": "All internal cross-repository declaration kinds",
      "source": "scripts/project_z.py:164-179,211-235,427-455",
      "result": "explicit_version is derived from declaration key presence, not from whether Cargo's normalized requirement looks restrictive. An explicit '*' remains true. validate applies the omission rule in the cross-repository branch without publish/kind/target/optional exemptions."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Aliases, target tables and workspace inheritance",
      "source": "scripts/project_z.py:164-179; tests/test_project_z.py:420-449",
      "result": "The extractor maps normal/dev/build tables, normalizes target cfg whitespace while preserving string literals, follows the Cargo alias, and reads the inherited workspace.dependencies entry. Direct and inherited target-alias declarations reach the same rejection, then become valid after only the version field is removed."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Same-repository path semantics",
      "source": "scripts/project_z.py:438-449; tests/test_project_z.py:174-211,388-403",
      "result": "Existing explicit version compatibility checks remain in the same-repository branch, including invalid/mismatched requirements. Path-only prerelease dependencies and exact intended workspace paths remain accepted; no blanket version ban is applied to same-repository dependencies."
    },
    {
      "subject": "External and unknown internal packages",
      "source": "scripts/project_z.py:431-437,577-632; tests/test_project_z.py:405-408,451-483",
      "result": "External packages not owned by the catalog retain their source/version policy. Unknown packages from a registered GitHub repository still fail, including alternate URL spelling, and the unchanged lock/resolution checks also reject them."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Source pin and lock constraints",
      "source": "scripts/project_z.py:451-453,577-632",
      "result": "Canonical default-branch Git URL, no cross-repository path/selectors, exact locked Git SHA and package-version identity checks remain unchanged. Removing development version selectors does not remove the lock's version or source validation."
    },
    {
      "subject": "88fa external release projection",
      "source": "scripts/release_projection.py:rewrite and MatchTests",
      "result": "All seven release implementation/test blobs are identical in base, candidate and inspected worktree. Compatible historical version+git requirements are still checked against the locked version before conversion to exact registry version; invalid/mismatched requirements and selectors are rejected. The changed docs distinguish development policy from historical staging compatibility."
    },
    {
      "subject": "Documentation scope",
      "source": "AGENTS.md; CONTRIBUTING.md; README.md; docs/release-projection.md",
      "result": "All four documents agree that only cross-repository internal development dependency declarations lose version. Package/lock versions, same-repository paths and external sources remain. Staging stays separate, unverified and non-publishing by default."
    }
